            "answer": "(A) $\\hat{k}$",
            "concept": "$\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b}$ is perpendicular to both $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$; unit vector $=\\dfrac{\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b}}{|\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b}|}$.",
            "steps": [
              {
                "do": "Take the cross product of the two vectors.",
                "math": "(\\hat{i}-\\hat{j})\\times(\\hat{i}+\\hat{j}) = \\begin{vmatrix} \\hat{i} & \\hat{j} & \\hat{k} \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\end{vmatrix}"
              },
              {
                "do": "Expand along the first row.",
                "math": "= \\hat{i}(0-0)-\\hat{j}(0-0)+\\hat{k}(1+1) = 2\\hat{k}"
              },
              {
                "do": "Divide by its magnitude $2$ to get the unit vector.",
                "math": "\\dfrac{2\\hat{k}}{2} = \\hat{k}",
                "marks": 1
              },
              {
                "do": "Hence the answer is option (A).",
                "why": "$-\\hat{k}$ also works, but it is not an option."
              }
            ],
            "mistake": "Picking (D): $\\dfrac{\\hat{i}+\\hat{j}}{\\sqrt{2}}$ is one of the given directions, not perpendicular to it."
          }
        },
